#!/usr/bin/env bash
# The admin step of taking a repository in; Colly runs it from this clone, on the Human's gh login, first without
# --apply, then with it after his one approval of the changes it prints:
#   bin/onboard-owner <owner/name> --id <repository id>            show what it would change, and change nothing
#   bin/onboard-owner <owner/name> --id <repository id> --apply    invite the agents' account (write), set the
#        factory's rulesets (no rewrite on any branch; on main, a bootstrap one until the kit lands, then the kit's
#        gate, which with the repository variable GATE_REVIEWER=entire requires verify, tier and Entire's check
#        Entire Gates instead of review and verdict), create the reviewer environment, and read it all back
#   options, one for each repository variable the kit reads (#210), set before the gate's ruleset, which follows the
#   reviewer being set; a value is printed only for the four, and an option left out leaves its variable as it is:
#        --runner <json>          GATE_RUNNER          the runner of main's jobs
#        --pr-runner <json>       GATE_PR_RUNNER       the runner of the candidate's verify
#        --trusted-runner <json>  GATE_TRUSTED_RUNNER  the runner of the jobs that hold the reviewer's credential
#        --reviewer claude|entire GATE_REVIEWER        which reviewer the gate runs
#   A runner is JSON, as fromJSON(vars.X) reads it in the workflows: "ubuntu-latest" or ["self-hosted","macOS"]. It
#   refuses, with nothing done, a self-hosted trusted runner that is the runner of main's or the candidate's jobs or shares
#   a label with it beyond self-hosted, the system and the architecture (kit/.gate/enforced-rules.md). It does not know
#   a repository's deploy jobs, so that half of the rule, no deploy on the trusted runner, stays with the Human.
# The id is the repository's own (gh api repos/<owner>/<name> --jq .id), so a typo or a renamed repository is refused.
# Colly runs it with --apply again once the kit pull request has merged, to put the kit's gate in; his approval of
# the kit pull request covers that. It never runs git or anything the repository holds. FACTORY_AGENT (default:
# tuan9288-agent) names the agents' account.
exec node "$(dirname "$0")/lib/owner.mjs" "$@"
